# Reactive Surface Final Implementation Lock - 2026-07-05

## Status

This document is the current implementation lock for the Reactive Surface system.

The 3RT / 50-slot always-active smoke from 2026-07-05 is **excluded from the implementation plan**. It remains only as a future feasibility record:

- Report: `reactive-surface-3rt-50slot-future-smoke-report-2026-07-05.md`
- Verdict: single-channel paths PASS, but three simultaneous Array-DI RT writer systems FAIL with Water-only output.
- Planning impact: do not design the first implementation around always-running Ground + Grass + Water Array-DI writer systems.

## Hard Scope

- BP-only for the first implementation and validation pass.
- Local player only.
- Multiplayer, split-screen, server replication, and remote-player reactive sources are out of scope.
- No Unreal Water Plugin.
- No AnimNotify.
- No production/gameplay C++.
- UnrealMCP is authoring/test tooling only; final content must not depend on UnrealMCP.
- No SceneCapture path.
- No NPC-side ticking reactive agent registry in the first pass.

## Core Architecture

The reactive system is controlled by the local player.

```text
Local Player Character
  -> BP_ReactiveSurfaceControllerActor
      - owns the reactive window
      - pulls nearby source transforms
      - evaluates channel gates
      - updates Niagara user params / arrays
      - owns RT sleep/wake/clear/reproject policy

Characters / NPCs / creatures
  -> no ticking reactive runtime controller by default
  -> optional passive authoring markers only
```

The controller uses a **pull model**. It reads sockets, passive bone-attached markers, or class presets from nearby characters. NPCs do not tick their own reactive logic in the first pass.

## Source Authoring

Use two practical source families.

### Ground Contact Sources

For Snow / Sand / Mud / Dust.

- Used for footprint/contact effects.
- Usually foot sockets or passive bone-attached marker components.
- Carries foot side, footprint texture index, radius, strength, and contact thresholds.
- Requires foot contact solving.
- May be authored as socket presets or passive components on bones.
- Passive components must not tick; the player controller reads them.

### Influence Sources

For Grass/Foliage and Water/Puddle.

- Used for position/velocity/radius/strength impulses.
- Can be placed on body bones, feet, wheels, or creature contact bones.
- Works for quadrupeds by adding more passive markers.
- Does not require AnimNotify.
- Passive components must not tick; the player controller reads them.

This matches the current component decision: components are collection/authoring markers, not autonomous ticking agents.

## Channel Decisions

### Ground

- Snow / Sand / Mud / Dust share one Ground RT.
- Snow and Sand are assumed not to coexist on the same surface in the first pass.
- Mud and Dust may coexist; differences are handled by stamp strength/media params first.
- Per-pixel MediaID is not first pass. It is an escape hatch if visual tests fail.
- New footprint stamps require strict tag/PhysMat gate.
- Leaving the PhysMat does not immediately stop RT maintenance. If Ground RT is active, window update, decay, and reproject/clear policy continue until empty.
- RT empty is based on `LastGroundStampTime + MaxGroundDecayTime`, not CPU RT readback.
- Snow/Sand use footprint mask textures, not circular stamps.
- Footprint texture conditions: uncompressed or sim-stage-safe format, sRGB off, yaw rotation in stamp space, left/right handling or mirror.

### Grass / Foliage

- Grass is an unconditional channel once `bGrassEnabled` and grounded/source conditions pass.
- No PhysMat gate.
- No foliage-existence query.
- Only opt-in foliage/grass materials sample the Grass RT.
- Input is position + velocity + bend radius/strength/falloff.
- Use two layers:
  - presence stamp for stationary body/feet intersection
  - movement trail for velocity-driven bending
- Grass sleep is effectively only for all-airborne, all-out-of-bounds, or `bGrassEnabled=false`.

### Water / Puddle

- No Unreal Water Plugin.
- No footprint texture.
- Input is world position, velocity, radius, strength, WaterZ/PuddleDepth.
- Water uses a project-owned current/previous ripple RT path.
- First attempt should prefer Grid2D previous-frame read; packed current/previous or RT ping-pong remain fallbacks.
- Puddles are controlled by `PuddleVolume + Weather MPC`.
- Puddle visual area and volume authority must match. Do not make purely visual puddles that receive no reactive volume.

## Niagara / RT Contracts

Validated contracts:

- Grid2D -> RT export path is viable with the DirectSet / TwoD / NumThreads style setup used in the smoke tests.
- Runtime Array DI is viable on GPU sim stage only through the 3-step chain:
  1. create Custom HLSL input
  2. rewire HLSL input to `Module.*`
  3. link `Module.*` to `User.*`
- Hidden/direct `User.*` wiring is banned for runtime DI control.
- Custom HLSL is allowed. BP-only means no production C++ runtime, not "no Niagara HLSL".
- Multi-source accumulation must happen in a single loop/accumulator, not multiple StackContext overwrite modules.
- Texture2D mask sampling in sim stage is viable for Ground footprint stamp.
- Sliding-window reprojection is technically viable via V4c Array DI 3-chain path.

Excluded from first implementation:

- Three always-active Array-DI RT writer systems for Ground + Grass + Water.
- Using the failed 3RT future smoke as a performance baseline.

## Slot / Budget Decisions

First-pass budgets:

| Channel | Slots | Reason |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Ground | 64 | 20 nearby characters x 2 feet plus landing/extra margin |
| Grass | 32 | body/contact influence sources |
| Water | 32 | body/contact ripple sources |

Selection rule:

- Collect nearby candidates.
- Sort by priority/distance.
- Push only the nearest/highest-priority budgeted sources.
- If more than the budget exists, the rest are not drawn.

Optimization rule:

- Do not draw every reactive effect all the time.
- Channel enabled switches gate whole channel work.
- Active count gates source injection.
- Sleep/wake is time-based.
- Grass can remain active more often because its presence layer is intentional, but it still obeys `bGrassEnabled` and bounds.
- Ground/Water should avoid unnecessary injection and should preserve/decay active RT state correctly.

## Sliding Window / Reprojection

Primary path:

- Use V4c-validated Array DI 3-chain hold+reproject.
- Derive divisor from runtime Grid2D NumCells, not RT size assumptions.
- Run a 1-cell self-check in fixture/integration.

Fallback path:

- Larger Ground window.
- Chunk-style recenter threshold.
- Fade/clear on recenter instead of hard pop where possible.

User gate still open:

- Phase 4 must decide whether the visual preservation level of old footprints is acceptable.

## Implementation Order

1. Controller + source authoring lock
   - `BP_ReactiveSurfaceControllerActor`
   - passive source markers / socket presets
   - Tick Group `TG_PostUpdateWork`
   - no AnimNotify

2. Grass vertical slice
   - simplest visual channel
   - position/velocity influence
   - opt-in material sampling

3. BP -> Niagara -> RT -> Material latency check
   - target is perceptually no delay, not mathematically same-frame guaranteed
   - use pre-contact threshold if a one-frame pipeline delay exists

4. Ground vertical slice
   - foot contact solver
   - footprint mask texture stamp
   - Snow/Sand first
   - Mud/Dust after base behavior works

5. Water/Puddle vertical slice
   - project water plane/volume
   - PuddleVolume + Weather MPC
   - current/previous ripple

6. Slot compaction / 20 nearby candidate pass
   - arrays use the proven 3-chain route
   - performance gate: BP tick budget target <= 1.0 ms for the collection/packing side

7. Integrated sleep/reproject/material/passive-marker cleanup
   - material V-flip/UV contract
   - RT lifecycle
   - packaging/dependency audit

## Remaining Gates

| Gate | Decision Needed |
| --- | --- |
| Footprint visual standard | Left/right mask textures, scale, yaw, and creature presets |
| Foot preservation feel | Phase 4 user approval for hold+reproject/fallback behavior |
| BP collection budget | Confirm <= 1.0 ms or reduce source counts/update rate |
| Water solver stability | Confirm no runaway ripple and acceptable material normal reconstruction |
| Production material opt-in | Ensure only intended materials sample each RT |

## Current Go / No-Go

Go for first implementation:

- BP-only local-player controller.
- Passive source markers/socket presets.
- Demand-driven channel activation.
- Ground footprint texture stamp.
- Grass influence field.
- Water/Puddle project-owned ripple RT.
- V4c hold+reproject as primary technical path.

No-Go for first implementation:

- Always-running 3RT Array-DI writer architecture.
- NPC-side ticking reactive components.
- Water Plugin dependency.
- AnimNotify dependency.
- Production C++ dependency.
- Multiplayer/replication scope.

